{"text": "CONGRESSMAN RICHARD E. NEAL\nCHAIR, HOUSE WAYS & MEANS COMMITTEE\n\nRichard E Neal for Congress Committee\nPO BOX 718 | SPRINGFIELD, MA 01101-0718\n(413) 842-6363 | INFO@NEALFORCONGRESS.COM\n\nSummary\n\nRichie Neal was first elected to the United States House of Representatives in 1988. Since January\n20109, he serves as Chairman of the powerful Committee on Ways and Means. Congressman Neal has\nspent his career fighting for things that matter to everyday Americans including access to affordable\nand dependable health care, a fair tax code, and the dependability of Social Security and Medicare\nbenefits.\n\nEducation\n\nSpringfield Technical High School, Springfield\nHolyoke Community College, Holyoke\nAmerican International College, Springfield \u2014 Bachelor of Arts, Political Science, 1972\n\nUniversity of Hartford's Barney School of Business and Public Administration, Hartford \u2014 Master of\nArts, Public Administration, 1976\n\nPublic Service\n\nCity Councilor, City of Springfield\nPresident of the City Council 1979\nIn office 1978-1983\n\nMayor, City of Springfield\nIn office 1983-1989\n\nU.S. Congressman\n2nd District \u2014 1989 to 2013; 1st District \u2014 2013 to present\nChairman Neal is the dean of both the Massachusetts Delegation and the New England\nCongressional Delegation, as well as an At-Large Whip for the House Democrats.\nCommittee Assignments\ne\u00a2 2007-2009: Committee on Ways and Means; Subcommittee on Oversight; Subcommittee on\nSocial Security\n\ne 2009-2011: Committee on Ways and Means; Subcommittee on Select Revenue Measures\n(Chairman)",
